  "problem": "The following table shows the width and length, in meters, of a rectangular storage warehouse.\n\n| Width | Length |\n| --- | --- |\n| $843$ | $1\\,617$ |\n\nRounding to the nearest hundred, determine the approximate ratio of width to length for this warehouse.",
  "worked_solution": "First, let's approximate the width and length by rounding to the nearest $100$:\n\n- width: $843⟶800$\n\n- length: $1\\,617⟶1\\,600$\n\nTherefore, the ratio of width to length (expressed as a fraction) is approximately\n\n$$\n\\frac{800}{1\\,600}.\n$$\n\nWe can simplify this ratio by dividing both numbers by $100$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{800÷100}{1\\,600÷100}=\\frac{8}{16}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide by $8$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{8÷8}{16÷8}=\\frac{1}{2}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the ratio of width to length is approximately $\\frac{1}{2}.$",
